title: UpdraftCentral RPC Request From Client Without UpdraftPlus User-Agent
id: 2b59774c-ccc0-486b-b71e-b7d6b52ce5c6
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects requests to the UpdraftCentral RPC endpoint (class-udrpc.php)
    that do not carry the UpdraftPlus client User-Agent. Attackers who stole
    UpdraftCentral connection keys sent signed remote commands from their own
    tooling to upload and activate backdoor plugins on connected WordPress
    sites, and those requests did not come from the plugin's own client.
references:
    - https://teamupdraft.com/blog/security-incident-october-2026/
    - https://nethemba.com/updraftcentral-backdoor-analysis/
    - https://patchstack.com/articles/updraftcentral-key-compromise-wordpress-backdoors/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/10/20
tags:
    - attack.t1078
    - attack.t1505
    - attack.t1199
logsource:
    category: webserver
    product: linux
detection:
    selection:
        cs-uri|contains: 'class-udrpc.php'
    filter_ua:
        cs-user-agent|contains: 'UpdraftPlus'
    condition: selection and not filter_ua
falsepositives:
    - Monitoring or backup automation that calls class-udrpc.php with a custom User-Agent
    - Older or third-party UpdraftCentral clients whose User-Agent does not contain UpdraftPlus
level: high
